    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33134" root="فحص" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَحْصٌ</span></b>  <i>Even ground; an expanded and open
tract:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُحُوصٌ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And hence, (TA,)
<i>Any inhabited place.</i> (K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  In a trad.
respecting the intercession [of Mohammad for his
people], where it is said, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَٱنْطَلَقَ حَتَّى أَتَى الفَحْصَ</span>
[<i>And he went away until he came to the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فحص</span>],
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفحص</span> is said to signify <i>What is before the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَرْش</span>
[<i>of God</i>]. (TA.)

